Hi to everyone!
While downloading the game, was reading plenty of reviews, would like to highlight the following:
- IT WORKS STABLE WITHOUT CRASHES;
- definately turn off MSAA, unless you have powerful 8gb (or more) graphics card;
- visuals, functionality, atmosphere looks and plays gorgeous;
- can't say much about the story (as I have only started), but sure, that it should be great and meaningful;
- previous game recap video is a nice choiche for the Deus Ex newcomers;
- I definately recomend it.
At this moment, playing on High config without tesselation, MSAA on 1980 x 1024, by benchmark having around 54 fps on average. By turning MSAA on 2x - around 37 fps on average.
My config:
Intel Core i5 4690k
MSI Z87-GD65
16 gb ddr3 2400
MSI R9 290 gaming 4g

All I see is people complaining about performance and the in-game store, here are two solutions;
Firstly turn os MSAA, this will drastically increase your performance, even me with a GTX 1080 can't handle MSAA, if you are still having performance issues then you simply need a more powerful rig.
Secondly the in-game store, ignore it, forget it exists and just get on with the game, you'll see it is actually good and that the in-game store has very little difference to the game and gameplay itself.

